  "title": "Anna Komnene",
  "summary": "Anna Komnene was born in 1083 in the Porphyra, the purple room of the imperial palace in Constantinople. She wrote the Alexiad in Greek, a history of her father Alexios I that covers 1069 to 1118. After her brother John II became emperor in 1118 she was sent to the Kecharitomene monastery, and she died around 1153.",
